+# Specification Quality Checklist: Accept the MCP Standard Metadata Field in Handoff Tool Calls
+
+**Purpose**: Validate specification completeness and quality before proceeding to planning
+**Created**: 2026-10-27
+**Feature**: [spec.md](../spec.md)
+
+## Content Quality
+
+- [x] No implementation details (languages, frameworks, APIs)
+  - Domain vocabulary only (`_meta`, MCP, stdio, tool call) is used because it is given by the problem; no language, framework, file-path, or code-structure choices are prescribed in the requirements.
+- [x] Focused on user value and business needs
+  - Centered on "native MCP clients can actually call handoff tools" plus "no guardrail is weakened" and "both deployments stay in parity."
+- [x] Written for non-technical stakeholders
+  - User stories and success criteria describe outcomes a stakeholder can reason about; the metadata object is described as opaque and dispatch-neutral.
+- [x] All mandatory sections completed
+  - User Scenarios & Testing, Requirements (Functional + Key Entities), Success Criteria, and Assumptions are all filled.
+
+## Requirement Completeness
+
+- [x] No [NEEDS CLARIFICATION] markers remain
+  - None present. Every open aspect was resolved with an informed default recorded under Assumptions.
+- [x] Requirements are testable and unambiguous
+  - Each FR states a capability plus its observable rejection/acceptance outcome; each maps to a concrete acceptance scenario.
+- [x] Success criteria are measurable
+  - SC-001..SC-004 use 100% / 0-regression / 100%-content-match / zero-difference targets that can be checked from tests and a content comparison.
+- [x] Success criteria are technology-agnostic (no implementation details)
