+# Contract: `tools/call` over MCP stdio (task-handoff adapter)
+
+**Feature**: 001-bench | **Date**: 2026-10-26 | **Wire**: newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdio
+
+Phase 1 of `/speckit.plan`. The task-handoff adapter exposes an external interface to other systems (native MCP clients): a newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 server over stdio (`task_handoff.py --mcp-stdio`). This contract documents the **changed** method's parameter acceptance rule in context of the **stable** surrounding envelope, so an implementer and a reviewer can verify both that `_meta` is now accepted and that nothing else moved (SC-004). Field semantics live in [`../data-model.md`](../data-model.md); this file is the wire-level observable contract only.
+
+## Transport frame rules (unchanged)
+
+- One JSON-RPC message per line, terminated by `\n`.
+- A physical frame longer than `MAX_MCP_MESSAGE` (`32 * 1024` bytes), or not ending in `\n`, is refused **before** JSON parsing with a single `id:null` error of code `-32600 invalid request`, the remaining bytes are never consumed as a second request, and no Runtime work is performed (FR-005). An oversized frame that also carries `_meta` is still refused by size first.
+
+## Envelope (stable)
+
+Every response is a single JSON object on one line, compact separators (`separators=(",", ":")`).
+
+- Success: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":<reqId>,"result":<result>}`
+- Error: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":<reqId>,"error":{"code":<int>,"message":<string>}}`
+
+Error codes used by this surface:
+
+| Code | Meaning | Raised when |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| `-32600` | invalid request | frame too large or unterminated (before parse); malformed envelope is otherwise `-32602`/`-32603`. |
+| `-32601` | method not found | unknown `method`. |
+| `-32602` | invalid request | `tools/call` `params` fail the closed-set / object / `_meta`-object guard below; or non-object envelope fields. |
+| `-32603` | internal error | unexpected exception while handling a request. |
+
+Note: a well-formed `tools/call` whose *arguments* are bad (unknown tool, missing required argument, unsupported argument key, identity override) does **not** become a transport error; it returns a **result** with `isError:true` and body text `handoff tool failed; result is unobserved`. Distinguish the two failure bands: **params-level** refusals → `-32602`; **tool-level** failures → `result.isError:true`.
+
+## Methods
+
+### `initialize` (unchanged)
+
+Request: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":<n>,"method":"initialize","params":{...}}`
+Result: `{"protocolVersion":"2025-06-18","capabilities":{"tools":{}},"serverInfo":{"name":"graphhelm-task-handoff","version":"0.1.11"}}`
+The `serverInfo.version` must equal `plugins/graphhelm/plugin.json` `version` (the test asserts this).
+
+### `ping` (unchanged)
+
+Request: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":<n>,"method":"ping"}`
+Result: `{}` (empty object).
+
+### `tools/list` (unchanged)
+
+Request: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":<n>,"method":"tools/list"}`
+Result: `{"tools":[{offer},{receive},{status}]}` — the closed three-tool surface with `additionalProperties:false` argument schemas (see data model `ToolArgumentSchema`).
+
+### `tools/call` (CHANGED — the subject of this feature)
+
+Request:
+```json
+{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":<n>,"method":"tools/call",
+ "params":{"name":"<offer|receive|status>","arguments":{...},"_meta":{...}}}
+```
+
+**Accepted `params` keys (closed set): `name`, `arguments`, `_meta`.** Any other key → `-32602` (unchanged guardrail, FR-003).
+
+**`_meta` acceptance rule (new):** optional. If present it MUST be a JSON object; if its value is any other JSON type (string, number, boolean, list, or `null`) → `-32602` before dispatch (FR-002). When present-and-an-object (including `{}`), it is accepted and **ignored for dispatch**: the dispatcher receives only `name`, `arguments`, and the process identity, so routing and argument interpretation are unchanged (FR-001, SC-001, SC-004).
+
+Result (success): `{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"<compact JSON of the tool result>"}],"isError":false}`
+Result (tool-level failure, e.g. unsupported argument key / identity override / missing required arg / unknown tool): `{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"handoff tool failed; result is unobserved"}],"isError":true}`
+
+## Worked examples (mirror the spec's acceptance scenarios)
+
+Each request is one stdin line. "No Runtime side effect" means zero HTTP calls reach the Runtime for params-level refusals.
+
+### 1. Metadata object accepted, dispatched as if absent — SC-001 / FR-001 (User Story 1)
+
+Request (progress token present):
+```json
+{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"status","arguments":{},"_meta":{"progressToken":"tok-1"}}}
+```
+Response: same as the no-metadata equivalent — `...,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\"format\":\"graphhelm-portable-v1\",\"phase\":\"status\",...}"}],"isError":false},...`
+
+### 2. Empty metadata object accepted — User Story 1, scenario 2
+
+Request:
+```json
+{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":4,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"status","arguments":{},"_meta":{}}}
+```
+Response: `result.isError:false`, identical shape to scenario 1 without `_meta`. Empty metadata has no effect on dispatch.
+
+### 3. Unknown field still refused even with valid `_meta` — FR-003 (User Story 2, scenario 3)
+
+Request:
+```json
+{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"status","arguments":{},"_meta":{},"bogus":1}}
+```
+Response: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":5,"error":{"code":-32602,"message":"invalid request"}}`
+A valid metadata object does not excuse another unknown key. No tool runs; no Runtime call.
+
+### 4. Non-object metadata refused — FR-002 (User Story 2, scenario 2)
+
+For each `badMeta` in `"a string"`, `7`, `true`, `[1]`, `null`:
+```json
+{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":6,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"status","arguments":{},"_meta":<badMeta>}}
+```
+Response: `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":6,"error":{"code":-32602,"message":"invalid request"}}` before dispatch. `null` is rejected (present key, not an object). No Runtime call.
+
+### 5. Identity override through arguments still refused — FR-004 (User Story 2, scenario 4)
+
+Request:
+```json
+{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":7,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"status","arguments":{"host":"claude"}}}
+```
+Response: `...,"result":{"content":[{"type":"text","text":"handoff tool failed; result is unobserved"}],"isError":true},...` (tool-level refusal because `host` is not in the `status` argument schema). Unchanged by this feature.
+
+### 6. Oversized frame refused before parse — FR-005 (User Story 2, scenario 5)
+
+A single frame of length `> MAX_MCP_MESSAGE` (with or without `_meta` inside it):
+Response: exactly one line `{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":null,"error":{"code":-32600,"message":"invalid request"}}`; process exits non-zero; no second request parsed; no Runtime call.
+
+### 7. Parity across deployments — FR-006 / SC-003 (User Story 3)
+
+Identical request bytes sent to either `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py --mcp-stdio` or `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/task_handoff.py --mcp-stdio` produce the same acceptance decision and the same result shape, because the two files are byte-identical (verified by equal SHA-256 — see `quickstart.md`).
+
+## Invariants of the change
+
+1. Only `name`, `arguments`, `_meta` are ever accepted as `params` keys; everything else stays refused.
+2. `_meta` presence changes only whether a call that previously read as "unsupported field" now proceeds to dispatch; for requests **without** `_meta`, every response is byte-for-byte identical to the pre-change behavior (SC-004).
+3. Refusals in steps 1–3 of the data-model decision flow occur before dispatch ⇒ no Runtime work.
+4. Dispatch consumes only `(name, arguments, identity)`; `_meta` is never forwarded, logged, persisted, or executed.
