+**Structure Decision**: In-place, minimal edits within the existing plugin layout. No new directory, module, package, or dependency is created (Keel "add only surface the promise needs"). The two `task_handoff.py` copies remain the single shared source of truth for the wire behavior, kept byte-identical.
+
+**Scope card (three-line, per Keel bounded-change route)**:
+- **Paths in scope**: `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/task_handoff.py`, `plugins/graphhelm-codex-hooks/hooks/task_handoff.py`, `plugins/graphhelm/hooks/test_task_handoff.py`.
+- **Promise**: A `tools/call` whose `params` are exactly `{name, arguments}` optionally plus an object-valued `_meta` is accepted and dispatched as if `_meta` were absent; any other `params` key, a non-object `_meta` (including `null`), an identity-override attempt through `arguments`, and an oversized frame are all still refused with no Runtime side effect; the two adapters stay byte-identical.
+- **Command that proves it**: `python -m unittest plugins.graphhelm.hooks.test_task_handoff` (full suite green, including the new `_meta` case) **and** an equal-SHA-256 comparison of the two `task_handoff.py` files (see `quickstart.md`).
